  "grade": "artifacts:control-sequence",
  "description": "What proto_version 0.7 adds to a connection's control socket, as closed shapes: `auth {kind: prompt}` and `connect.login_timeout` (integer milliseconds, 10000 to 1800000, sent only with a prompt-mode connect to a peer at 0.7 or later); the events `hostkey_ask` and `auth_prompt` (`banner`, `password`, `keyboard-interactive`); the commands `hostkey_answer` and `auth_answer`; `auth_failed.code`; `error` code `hostkey_refused` in the branch without a session. The schema checks each field's shape; that a prompt-mode connect carries `login_timeout`, and the order of the rest, are the control-sequence check's and the worker's tests. An `auth_prompt` is `prompt_id` exactly when it has prompts. Every credential-shaped value is the synthetic constant.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.4",
    "open_decisions §5",
    "device-login steps 10 to 18",
    "ipc-control rules 1 to 8"
  ],
